IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Civil Dispute Resolution Act 2011 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2011A00017.txt (compilation
-- No. 4, 14 October 2024). Parts 2-5 commenced on 1 August 2011. The party to
-- a civil case asks: "Must I file a genuine steps statement, by when, and what
-- if I do not?"

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `My side` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the respondent`

-- s 5 eligible court.
DECLARE `Court` IS ONE OF
    `the Federal Court of Australia`
    `the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)`
    `another court`

-- ss 15-17: the kinds of excluded proceedings.
DECLARE `Kind of proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `ordinary civil proceedings`
    `for a pecuniary penalty for a civil penalty provision`
    `by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority connected with an offence or civil penalty contravention`
    `relating to a decision of, or reviewed by, a listed tribunal or prescribed body`
    `in the appellate jurisdiction`
    `arising from a power to compel answers, documents or appearance`
    `about issuing or executing a warrant`
    `involving a declared vexatious litigant`
    `ex parte`
    `to enforce an enforceable undertaking`
    `under a listed Act, such as the Fair Work, Family Law or Migration Act`
    `within the jurisdiction of the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 1), or Division 2 under section 132`
    `prescribed by the regulations`

DECLARE `Dispute case` HAS
    `my side`                                               IS A `My side`
    `the court`                                             IS A `Court`
    `the proceedings are civil`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the kind of proceedings`                               IS A `Kind of proceedings`
    -- ss 6(3)-(4): "to the extent that"
    `only part of the proceedings is of that kind`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the application is filed`                      IS A DATE
    -- s 7(1)
    `I was given a copy of the applicant's statement`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the hearing date specified in the application`         IS A DATE

DECLARE `Dispute position` HAS
    `I must file a genuine steps statement`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day to file it`                               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `it may leave out the excluded parts`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `not filing invalidates the proceedings`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court may weigh my steps and statement, including on costs` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

@ref s 5 eligible court
GIVEN c IS A `Dispute case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court is eligible` c IF
    NOT (c's `the court` EQUALS `another court`)

-- ss 15-17: excluded "to the extent that" they are of a listed kind.
@ref ss 15-17
GIVEN c IS A `Dispute case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceedings are of an excluded kind` c IF
    NOT (c's `the kind of proceedings` EQUALS `ordinary civil proceedings`)

@ref s 6(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Dispute case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceedings are wholly excluded` c IF
        `the proceedings are of an excluded kind` c
    AND NOT (c's `only part of the proceedings is of that kind`)

-- s 6(1), (3)-(4): the applicant in civil proceedings in an eligible court,
-- unless wholly excluded. s 7(1): a respondent given a copy of the applicant's
-- statement; the s 6(3) exclusion does not reach s 7 (F5). Part 2 commenced on
-- 1 August 2011 (s 2, item 2). Both changed after the independent pass.
@ref ss 6(1), (3)-(4), 7(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Dispute case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must file` c IF
        `the court is eligible` c
    AND c's `the proceedings are civil`
    AND c's `the day the application is filed` AT LEAST Date 1 8 2011
    AND (   (c's `my side` EQUALS `the applicant` AND NOT (`the proceedings are wholly excluded` c))
         OR (c's `my side` EQUALS `the respondent` AND c's `I was given a copy of the applicant's statement`))

-- s 6(1): "at the time of filing the application"; s 7(1): "before the
-- hearing date specified in the application", so the day before it at latest.
@ref ss 6(1), 7(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Dispute case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to file for` c MEANS
    IF NOT (`I must file` c)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF c's `my side` EQUALS `the applicant`
         THEN JUST (c's `the day the application is filed`)
         ELSE JUST (`the day before` (c's `the hearing date specified in the application`))

-- s 6(4): it need not relate to the excluded parts.
@ref s 6(4)
GIVEN c IS A `Dispute case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it may leave out excluded parts` c IF
        `I must file` c
    AND c's `my side` EQUALS `the applicant`
    AND `the proceedings are of an excluded kind` c

-- s 10(2): failure does not invalidate the application, a response or the
-- proceedings. ss 11-12: the court may take account of whether a person
-- required to file did so and took genuine steps, including in costs.
@ref ss 10(2), 11, 12(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Dispute case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may weigh it` c IF `I must file` c

@ref ss 4-7, 10-12, 15-17
@export default The position of a party to civil proceedings in the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) under the Civil Dispute Resolution Act 2011 (Cth): whether they must file a genuine steps statement (the applicant, when filing the application; a respondent given the applicant's statement, before the hearing date: ss 6-7), unless the proceedings are wholly excluded (ss 15-17; a statement in part-excluded proceedings may leave out the excluded parts, s 6(4)); that failing to file does not invalidate the proceedings (s 10(2)); and that the court may take account of whether they filed and took genuine steps, including in awarding costs (ss 11-12). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Dispute case`  @desc My side, the court, the kind of proceedings, the filing day, and for a respondent the copy and the hearing date
GIVETH A `Dispute position`
`the dispute position for` c MEANS
    `Dispute position` OF `I must file` c, `the last day to file for` c, `it may leave out excluded parts` c, FALSE, `the court may weigh it` c
